// @test: soft() over a struct `our<T>` still yields a weak handle that observes the drop (#427 defect 2, positive side)
// @description: the counterpart to test_soft_primitive_refused.vyb: `soft(our(A { v: 5 }))` takes a
//   weak count on the temporary's control block, the temporary's strong ref is dropped by soft()
//   itself, and the returned `mild<A>` therefore reports released=true -- the object was freed while
//   the weak handle lives on. A struct payload is heap-boxed and control-block backed, so the
//   primitive refusal must not touch it.
// @category: ownership
// @expect-output: released=true
// @expect-return: 0

share(all)
struct A { v<Int> }

main()<Int> -> {
    m<mild<A>> = soft(our(A { v: 5 }))
    println("released=" + m.released().to_string())
    return 0
}
